Context
Different tenants require different SLA rules (e.g., 24-hour resolution for banking fraud complaints, 72-hour for telecom outages). SLA logic must be flexible, configurable, and auditable.

Decision
Use an SLA Calculator module that computes due dates and priority from a tenant-specific SLA_CONFIG table.

Rationale
Centralises SLA logic in a single component
Supports tenant-specific variations without branching code
Easy to test and evolve
Works cleanly with Workflow Engine and ComplaintService

Consequences
Complaints must always resolve category/channel → SLA_CONFIG mapping
Incorrect configuration can affect priority calculations
Requires validation on admin-side SLA updates

Alternatives Considered
Hard-coding SLA rules → unmaintainable
Storing SLA rules in code → requires redeploy on every tenant change
